// Tests for Vale alerts inside \table blocks.
//
// BUG A — table_block line shift (Pass 2):
//   qdocCollectProse skips table_block without preserving newlines.
//   Prose after \endtable is reported N lines too early, where N = number of
//   lines inside the \table...\endtable block.
//   Fixed by emitting a '\n' per table line when skipping the block.
//
// BUG B — inside-table off-by-one (Pass 1):
//   Text nodes inside \table cells have StartPoint.Row one line later than
//   the \li line that introduces them, so alerts are reported one line low.

/*!
    \class QPluginLoader
    \brief Loads a plugin at run-time.

    \table
      \header
        \li Property \li Behavior
      \row
        \li fileName
        \li The plugin is loaded from this path on disk.
      \row
        \li isLoaded
        \li Returns \c true if the plugin was loaded successfully.
      \row
        \li loadHints
        \li Hints are used to control how the plugin is resolved.
    \endtable

    The loader is used to resolve symbols exported by the plugin.
    We recommend calling unload() when the plugin is no longer required.
*/
// Expected (after fixes):
//   25: Microsoft.Passive 'is loaded'              (inside table — BUG B: currently 26)
//   28: Microsoft.Passive 'was loaded'             (inside table — BUG B: currently 29)
//   31: Microsoft.Passive 'are used', 'is resolved' (inside table — BUG B: currently 32)
//   34: Microsoft.Passive 'is used'                (post-table — BUG A: currently 22)
//   35: Microsoft.We      'We'                     (post-table — BUG A: currently 23)

// Table test — passive voice in a multi-line \li cell.
//   Source: deployment-plugins.qdoc.
//   'are listed' is on a continuation line of a multi-line \li cell; Vale misses
//   it entirely (false negative: only the first line of a \li cell is linted).
//   'are built' is on a standalone \li and fires at the correct line.

/*!
    \page deployment-plugins-test.html
    \title Deploying Plugins Test
    \brief Tests for passive voice in table cells.

    \table
      \header
        \li Problem \li Cause \li Solution
      \row
        \li Plugins silently fail to load even when opened directly by the application.
            Qt Designer shows the plugin libraries in its Help|About Plugins dialog, but no
            plugins are listed under each of them.
        \li The application and its plugins are built in different modes.
        \li Build the plugin in the same configuration as the executable.
    \endtable
*/
// Current behavior:
//   61: Microsoft.Passive 'are listed'  — NOT reported (false negative: continuation line of \li not linted)
//   62: Microsoft.Passive 'are built'   — reported correctly
// Expected (after fix):
//   61: Microsoft.Passive 'are listed'  (continuation lines of \li cells should be linted)
//   62: Microsoft.Passive 'are built'   (unchanged — already correct)
